---Defines where users exist in the LDAP directory.
---@class gcp.gkehub_v2.IdentityServiceUserConfig
---@field loginAttribute? string Optional. The name of the attribute which matches against the input username. This is used to find the user in the LDAP database e.g. "(=)" and is combined with the optional filter field. This defaults to "userPrincipalName".
---@field filter? string Optional. Filter to apply when searching for the user. This can be used to further restrict the user accounts which are allowed to login. This defaults to "(objectClass=User)".
---@field idAttribute? string Optional. Determines which attribute to use as the user's identity after they are authenticated. This is distinct from the loginAttribute field to allow users to login with a username, but then have their actual identifier be an email address or full Distinguished Name (DN). For example, setting loginAttribute to "sAMAccountName" and identifierAttribute to "userPrincipalName" would allow a user to login as "bsmith", but actual RBAC policies for the user would be written as "bsmith@example.com". Using "userPrincipalName" is recommended since this will be unique for each user. This defaults to "userPrincipalName".
---@field baseDn? string Required. The location of the subtree in the LDAP directory to search for user entries.

